<$TOP/mkfiles/mkfile.proto

O=z
CC=zc
LD=zl -H7
AS=za
AR=iar

CFLAGS=$CFLAGS_COMMON -I$TOP/include/arch/alpha

# see mkfiles/386/mkfile's identical ARCHEXTRAOFILES comment. No
# getcallerpc.$O (unlike the original import's ARCHEXTRAOFILES, which
# listed one that never existed): alpha isn't excluded from
# port/getcallerpc.c's own #ifdef (only cputype386/amd64/arm get a
# real per-arch implementation there), so the portable `return 0;`
# fallback already applies here, same as arm64/mips/riscv/riscv64.
#
# div.$O: real Alpha hardware has no integer divide instruction at
# all (unlike arm, whose own div.$O is the same kind of gap but for a
# different reason -- see that mkfile's own comment), so zc's ADIVQ/
# AMODQ/ADIVL/AMODL pseudo-ops get expanded by linkers/zl/noop.c's own
# divsubr() into a JSR to _divq/_modq/_divl/_modl (etc, looked up by
# name) -- see arch/alpha/div.s's own header comment.
ARCHEXTRAOFILES=arch/alpha/setjmp.$O arch/alpha/div.$O
